WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.230
Off the coast of Queensland,
in north-east Australia,

2
00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:08.730
lies a marine park of
344,400 square kilometres.

3
00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:15.210
It holds about 3,000 coral reefs, and has
been a World Heritage site since 1981.

4
00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:18.830
It is worth about 9 billion Australian
dollars a year to Australia,

5
00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:22.410
and 77,000 full-time jobs.

6
00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:26.690
A marine park authority manages it,
working with the Queensland Government.

7
00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:31.870
So can rules made for the reef protect
it from threats that start far away?

8
00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.290
Or should tourists be banned?

9
00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:37.890
In this mission, you'll uncover
the threats the reef faces.

10
00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:42.170
Then you'll judge how it is managed,
and whether that is sustainable.

11
00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:46.920
Your mission: decide whether local rules
can protect the Great Barrier Reef.
